spilled some water over it

01:08:07.612 --> 01:08:08.559
or something.
- It was Red Bull.

01:08:08.559 --> 01:08:09.392
I remember her--
- Was it Red Bull?

01:08:09.392 --> 01:08:11.374
- Yeah I remember her being
like paranoid in the group chat

01:08:11.374 --> 01:08:14.374
being like, "How do I clean
red bull from the tatami mat?"

01:08:14.374 --> 01:08:15.952
(laughs)

01:08:15.952 --> 01:08:19.116
Yeah, that is the most, like
I-just-moved-to-Japan post.

01:08:19.116 --> 01:08:20.527
(laughs)

01:08:20.527 --> 01:08:22.724
- Us like Japan life.

01:08:22.724 --> 01:08:24.898
- Because as a foreigner
you just don't know

01:08:24.898 --> 01:08:26.561
how to deal with tatami rooms, right?

01:08:26.561 --> 01:08:28.491
So I'm like, "Can we
put furniture in here?

01:08:28.491 --> 01:08:29.747
"How the fuck can we
put anything in here?"

01:08:29.747 --> 01:08:30.580
You know what I mean?

01:08:30.580 --> 01:08:32.351
- Have you ever lived in a tatami room?

01:08:32.351 --> 01:08:33.291
- I have actually.

01:08:33.291 --> 01:08:34.174
- Did you like it?

01:08:34.174 --> 01:08:35.846
- Back in the day.

01:08:35.846 --> 01:08:38.277
Not really, I mean, it wasn't
quite my choice, was it?

01:08:38.277 --> 01:08:41.357
Because I recall back in the day

01:08:41.357 --> 01:08:43.788
I kind of didn't get to
choose where I lived.

01:08:43.788 --> 01:08:46.001
I was moving to a new city

01:08:46.001 --> 01:08:48.486
and they were just kinda
like, "Okay, go here.

01:08:48.486 --> 01:08:49.472
"This is your place."

01:08:49.472 --> 01:08:51.330
And I waltz in, it was super old.

01:08:51.330 --> 01:08:54.171
The walls were actually kind
of crumbling on the inside,

01:08:54.171 --> 01:08:56.929
there was a really
ancient tatami, actually.

01:08:56.929 --> 01:08:58.119
I already had water damage.

01:08:58.119 --> 01:09:01.707
So I went ahead and a water
damaged it a little bit more

01:09:01.707 --> 01:09:02.772
by actually...

01:09:02.772 --> 01:09:03.605
What I did was

01:09:03.605 --> 01:09:06.688
I was trying to figure
out how to dry my clothing

01:09:06.688 --> 01:09:09.233
because I had a washer outside

01:09:09.233 --> 01:09:10.998
and I washed my clothing there

01:09:10.998 --> 01:09:14.294
and it was kind of my first
experience in this kind of room.

01:09:14.294 --> 01:09:15.127
And I thought to myself,

01:09:15.127 --> 01:09:16.936
"Well, I have to hang these to dry, right?

01:09:16.936 --> 01:09:18.424
"Okay, I'll just do it in my house."

01:09:18.424 --> 01:09:20.787
So I hung it up and it was dripping.

01:09:20.787 --> 01:09:22.118
And so...
(murmurs)

01:09:22.118 --> 01:09:23.552
Yeah, so I went ahead and I went to sleep

01:09:23.552 --> 01:09:25.807
and I woke up and I thought to
myself, "What is that scent?

01:09:25.807 --> 01:09:26.962
(sniffs)

01:09:26.962 --> 01:09:28.300
"What is that scent in my home?"

01:09:28.300 --> 01:09:29.765
And then I looked over to the side

01:09:29.765 --> 01:09:32.356
and I looked at the dark
spot on the tatami mat

01:09:32.356 --> 01:09:33.587
and I thought, "Oh, I see."

01:09:33.587 --> 01:09:34.603
- Oh that's weird.

01:09:34.603 --> 01:09:35.436
(laughs)

01:09:35.436 --> 01:09:36.931
- The good news is I just kind of ran away

01:09:36.931 --> 01:09:38.617
and that was this.

01:09:38.617 --> 01:09:39.709
- It's your problem now.

01:09:39.709 --> 01:09:41.137
- One thing I will say though

01:09:41.137 --> 01:09:43.741
that not many foreigners get to experience

01:09:43.741 --> 01:09:45.707
is sleeping on a futon.

01:09:45.707 --> 01:09:49.041
And I will say sleeping on a
futon in a to tatami mat room

01:09:49.041 --> 01:09:50.220
is like--
- It's nice.

01:09:50.220 --> 01:09:51.820
- It's the best night of sleep I ever get.

01:09:51.820 --> 01:09:53.154
- Yeah, it's not bad.
- I don't know

01:09:53.154 --> 01:09:56.327
what it is about the feeling
of just sleeping on the floor.

01:09:56.327 --> 01:09:57.835
I don't know, it kind of
reminds me of grandma,

01:09:57.835 --> 01:09:59.379
like sleeping at grandma's
house or something like that.

01:09:59.379 --> 01:10:01.813
- I love, I personally
loved the tatami rooms.

01:10:01.813 --> 01:10:03.401
- When Garnt first told
me that he loved it,

01:10:03.401 --> 01:10:04.893
I was just like that meme of like,

01:10:04.893 --> 01:10:07.318
"Is this some peasant joke,

01:10:07.318 --> 01:10:08.151
"I'm too rich to understand?"

01:10:08.151 --> 01:10:09.253
Is that the meme?

01:10:09.253 --> 01:10:10.513
- Yeah, "Is this some peasant joke

01:10:10.513 --> 01:10:12.357
"I'm too rich to understand?"

01:10:12.357 --> 01:10:13.557
- 'Cause I have an old tatami room.

01:10:13.557 --> 01:10:14.866
Like why would I
voluntarily sleep on that?

01:10:14.866 --> 01:10:15.876
I have a bedroom bed.

01:10:15.876 --> 01:10:17.777
- I don't know, man, like, cause like...

01:10:17.777 --> 01:10:18.696
- I like it now.

01:10:18.696 --> 01:10:19.529
- Yeah.

01:10:19.529 --> 01:10:21.991
- 'Cause when we get a real
count we're forced to stay.

01:10:21.991 --> 01:10:24.438
- Like you know, my grandma's
house was nothing but tatami,

01:10:24.438 --> 01:10:26.514
'cause it was in the middle
of blood fuck nowhere

01:10:26.514 --> 01:10:28.204
in like the Japanese countryside.

01:10:28.204 --> 01:10:30.291
And sleep like just lying down on that

01:10:30.291 --> 01:10:32.024
in like on a summer day

01:10:32.024 --> 01:10:33.743
is like the best fucking
nap you'll ever take.

01:10:33.743 --> 01:10:35.865
- Feel like it did wonders for my back.

01:10:35.865 --> 01:10:36.730
- Oh yeah.
- Yes.

01:10:36.730 --> 01:10:38.076
It is good for your back
- It straightens it out.

01:10:38.076 --> 01:10:39.816
- It's strange to think about that.

01:10:39.816 --> 01:10:42.953
Sleeping on the floor is like more like...

01:10:42.953 --> 01:10:45.116
It feels more healthy
for your back and stuff

01:10:45.116 --> 01:10:47.713
than sleeping on a bed elevated.

01:10:47.713 --> 01:10:49.147
- Yeah, it is weird, right?

01:10:49.147 --> 01:10:51.101
It's kind of an oxymoronic almost.

01:10:51.101 --> 01:10:52.173
- Yeah.

01:10:52.173 --> 01:10:54.870
- That like somehow the most
uncomfortable sleeping...

01:10:54.870 --> 01:10:56.792
- That's how humans have been sleeping

01:10:56.792 --> 01:10:57.709
for like most of...

01:10:57.709 --> 01:10:58.976
- Alright Garnt, fucking nerd.

01:10:58.976 --> 01:11:00.755
- We're going back to
the Neanderthal phase

01:11:00.755 --> 01:11:02.952
sleeping on the ground.

01:11:02.952 --> 01:11:05.608
- So were you an anime
fan or anything as well?

01:11:05.608 --> 01:11:09.492
- Well, I used to watch
anime way back in the day.

01:11:09.492 --> 01:11:13.260
I would have to say,
I've seen a lot from...

01:11:13.260 --> 01:11:14.093
Let's see.

01:11:14.093 --> 01:11:17.225
Maybe, like 2010s, I would say.

01:11:17.225 --> 01:11:19.967
But the most recent anime
that I've really enjoyed

01:11:19.967 --> 01:11:22.762
is I think I really liked Dr. Stone,

01:11:22.762 --> 01:11:23.743
I've mentioned Dr. Stone.

01:11:23.743 --> 01:11:24.881
I really liked Made in Abyss.

01:11:24.881 --> 01:11:27.758
So those were the two
that I was really into.

01:11:27.758 --> 01:11:28.995
- We know that we know the guy

01:11:28.995 --> 01:11:31.181
who did the soundtrack to Made in Abyss.

01:11:31.181 --> 01:11:32.252
- Really you know?
- Yeah.

01:11:32.252 --> 01:11:33.480
- What, I love--
- Shout out...

01:11:33.480 --> 01:11:35.172
- Shout out to Kevin.

01:11:35.172 --> 01:11:36.005
- Heh!

01:11:36.005 --> 01:11:37.980
Wait. I love the soundtrack too.

01:11:37.980 --> 01:11:39.021
(laughs)

01:11:39.021 --> 01:11:41.422
- He's just this really Aussie bloke.

01:11:41.422 --> 01:11:42.604
(laughs)
- Yeah.

01:11:42.604 --> 01:11:45.042
You won't be amazed if you
ever meet him in real life.

01:11:45.042 --> 01:11:45.875
- Oh yeah?

01:11:45.875 --> 01:11:46.920
- He's just a normal Australian dude.

01:11:46.920 --> 01:11:49.123
- He's just the most
normal Australian dude.

01:11:49.123 --> 01:11:50.986
He was just like, yeah,
I did it Made in Abyss.

01:11:50.986 --> 01:11:52.693
- We'll look at drunk
with him. It'll be fine.

01:11:52.693 --> 01:11:53.526
- Yeah.
- Oh my God.

01:11:53.526 --> 01:11:54.909
That's awesome.

01:11:54.909 --> 01:11:55.925
- Dr. Stone, yeah I mean like--

01:11:55.925 --> 01:11:57.626
- I kind of thought that
Dr. Stone anime was mid.

01:11:57.626 --> 01:11:58.465
There I said it.

01:11:58.465 --> 01:11:59.353
Thought it was mediocre.

01:11:59.353 --> 01:12:01.133
- Oh that's okay. I can
totally understand that.

01:12:01.133 --> 01:12:02.326
I don't really know why I enjoyed it.

01:12:02.326 --> 01:12:05.381
I think my method of thought at that time

01:12:05.381 --> 01:12:07.828
was, "I haven't watched
anime in a long time.

01:12:07.828 --> 01:12:08.769
"Let's just watch something.

01:12:08.769 --> 01:12:10.834
"This guy has a head that
looks like a piece of celery.

01:12:10.834 --> 01:12:12.875
"Let's just go into it."

01:12:12.875 --> 01:12:15.225
And I checked it out and I
really liked the main character.

01:12:15.225 --> 01:12:16.352
He made me laugh a lot.

01:12:16.352 --> 01:12:20.473
He has like a personality
that I enjoy and yeah.

01:12:20.473 --> 01:12:22.479
I mean, I think the characters are fine,

01:12:22.479 --> 01:12:24.226
but I don't know what it was.

01:12:24.226 --> 01:12:25.396
I think just...

01:12:25.396 --> 01:12:26.829
It was a nice comfy show

01:12:26.829 --> 01:12:27.787
that I could sit back and not really care

01:12:27.787 --> 01:12:28.644
too much about.
- I agree with that, yeah.

01:12:28.644 --> 01:12:30.078
- It was definitely comfy.

01:12:30.078 --> 01:12:31.654
- I did because everyone was hyping it up

01:12:31.654 --> 01:12:34.182
it's like the next big show.

01:12:34.182 --> 01:12:35.880
- It's really weird
right 'cause I think...

01:12:35.880 --> 01:12:38.328
I think the thing I didn't like about it

01:12:38.328 --> 01:12:39.529
was the Shonen side.

01:12:39.529 --> 01:12:43.178
The fact that it was like a
typical Shonen Jump anime.

01:12:43.178 --> 01:12:44.214
And what I didn't like

01:12:44.214 --> 01:12:46.432
was when they had like
these arbitrary battles

01:12:46.432 --> 01:12:47.338
and stuff like that.

01:12:47.338 --> 01:12:48.563
Like I saw the tournament talk

01:12:48.563 --> 01:12:50.008
and it was the first time I was like,

01:12:50.008 --> 01:12:51.683
"Why is there a tournament?

01:12:51.683 --> 01:12:52.806
"Please get rid of the tournament."

01:12:52.806 --> 01:12:54.371
- It's true. That was so bad.

01:12:54.371 --> 01:12:56.592
It was like, "Just get back
to the science, I liked that."

01:12:56.592 --> 01:12:58.801
- Boo! Get back to the science.

01:12:58.801 --> 01:13:00.009
We want the science.

01:13:00.009 --> 01:13:02.656
Whenever they were just
inventing stuff like that scene

01:13:02.656 --> 01:13:06.649
where they invent the light
bulb, fucking brilliant scene.

01:13:06.649 --> 01:13:09.117
- Yeah. That was awesome,
I love that kind of stuff.

01:13:09.117 --> 01:13:10.702
- But like when they're
fighting, I'm like,

01:13:10.702 --> 01:13:12.519
"Get this shit outta me."

01:13:12.519 --> 01:13:13.631
